1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, vê carê jî em li berxwe da navçeya
Mabeta.
 
Yes, dear viewers, this time we have headed to the Mabeta
district.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vê carê jî em ê derbasî du gundan bibin, du gund bûne yek.
 
This time we will visit two villages, two villages that have
become one.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Gundê Êlî Caro û gundê Raca.
 
The village of Êlî Caro and the village of Raca.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Dike ku ev heftê jî em bi hev re derbas bikin.
 
So that we will spend this week together as well.

5
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, îro jî em derbasî gundê Raca û Êlî
Caro bûn.
 
Yes, dear viewers, today we passed into the village of Raca
and Êlî Caro.

6
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Îro jî em derbasî du gundan bûne, milletekî herdu gundan jî
li hev kom bûne.
 
Today we visited two villages, the people of both villages
have gathered together.

7
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Naha jî em li gundê Raca ne. Naha jî em ê di rûkê her
gundekî nas bikin.
 
Right now we are in the village of Raca. Now we will get to
know the elders of each village.

8
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Merheba ji we re.
 
Hello to you.

9
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Ehlan wa sehlan bi hatina we, hûn bi xêr hatine ser çavê
min.
 
Welcome, you've brought joy by coming, you are welcome upon
my eyes.

10
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Spas, em destpêkê te nas bikin?
 
Thank you, can we get to know you first?

11
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Navê min Mistefa ye, lawê Hecî 'Eme, ji Êlî Caro.
 
My name is Mustafa, son of Hacı Eme, from Êlî Caro.

12
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Ser çavên min. Tu ji Êlî Caro yî.
 
Upon my eyes. You are from Êlî Caro.

13
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

14
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Êlî Caro nav ji ku hatiye?
 
Where did the name Êlî Caro come from?

15
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Bixwe Jaro ye. Navê lê bûye Êlî. Bi Kurmancî kirin Êlî Jaro.
 
Actually it's Jaro. His name was Êlî. In Kurmanji they made
it Êlî Jaro.

16
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Bi Erebî dibêjin Ali Jaro, bi Kurmancî jî dibêjin Êlî Jaro.
 
In Arabic they say Ali Jaro, and in Kurmanji they say Êlî
Jaro.

17
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Naha ji ber ku gundê we û Raca jî gihîştine hev, du gund
bûne yek, dema ku em derbasî gund bûn, mirov nizane kîjan
gund e, Êlî Caro ye an Raca ye, rast e an na?
 
Now, because your village and Raca have merged and become
one, when we entered the village, you wouldn't know which
village it is, whether it's Êlî Caro or Raca, is that right
or not?

18
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Mabeyna me, Êlî Caro û Raca, bes camî ye.
 
Between us, Êlî Caro and Raca, there is only a mosque.

19
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Hêla camiyê ya xerbî Êlî Caro ye, hêla rojhilatê şerqî Raca
ye.
 
The western side of the mosque is Êlî Caro, the eastern side
is Raca.

20
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Yanî bes camî di ortê me de ye. Wekî din gundê me yek e.
 
So, it's just the mosque in between us. Otherwise, our
village is one.

21
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Ê naha Êlî Caro... malbat yek e, an malbatên din jî hene?
 
And now Êlî Caro... is the family one, or are there other
families as well?

22
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Bixwe mala Hesên e, mala Hec Birîm, mala 'Eme, mala Ehmed,
mala Şêx e.
 
Actually, there is the house of Hesen, the house of Hec
Birim, the house of Eme, the house of Ehmed, and the house
of Şêx.

23
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Evana esasê wan yek in. Evna gişt ji Êlî Jaro ne. Yanî gişt
yek in, aîle yek e.
 
These share one origin. They are all from Êlî Jaro. So they
are all one, it's one family.

24
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Wekî din pismam, dotmam, xwarzî... tevlîhev bûne.
 
Other than that, paternal cousins, maternal cousins,
nephews... they've intermingled.

25
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Dibistan jî yek e?
 
Is the school also one?

26
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Dibistan sala 1958'an da hat girtin. Kalê min mixtar bû wî
jî ew girtin, sala 1958'an.
 
The school was opened in 1958. My grandfather was the
headman and he opened it, in 1958.

27
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Ku qeçkê me diçûn Koxrê dixwendin, dema ev girtin e zarok
dihatin mekteba me dixwendin.
 
When our children used to go to Koxrê to study, when this
was opened, children would come study at our school.

28
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Pênc gundan li vê derê dixwend heta sefa çaran.
 
Five villages would study here until the fourth grade.

29
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Yanî dibistan yek e, mizgeft yek e, cîranî yek e... yanî hûn
hemî bi hev re ne.
 
So the school is one, the mosque is one, the neighborhood is
one... meaning you are all together.

30
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Mabeyna me û Raca, gişt yek e. Heta naha komîna me yek e.
 
Between us and Raca, it's all one. Even now our commune is
one.

31
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Komîn jî yek e? Navê komîna we li ser kîjan şehîdî ye?
 
The commune is also one? Which martyr is your commune named
after?

32
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Bixwe şehîd Xoşnav, navê komîna me ye.
 
Actually, Martyr Xoşnav is the name of our commune.

33
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Spas xalê min, spas. Ê merheba ji te re jî.
 
Thank you, uncle, thank you. And hello to you too.

34
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Merheba, ehlen wa sehlen. Em bi we jî.
 
Hello, welcome. Us to you as well.

35
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Em te jî nas bikin destpêkê?
 
Can we get to know you as well, to begin?

36
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Elî Hemê.
 
Elî Hemê.

37
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Ser çavê min, tu ji Raca yî?
 
Upon my eyes, are you from Raca?

38
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Erê ez ji Raca me.
 
Yes, I am from Raca.

39
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Ê ka ji me re li ser Raca bisekine, gundê Raca ji kengî ve
çêbûye, nav ji ku hatiye?
 
Well, tell us about Raca, since when was the village of Raca
established, where did the name come from?

40
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Ya sîdî, Raca bixwe, lewê Çomazin e, Raca.
 
Well, my good sir, Raca itself is a descendant of Çomazin,
Raca.

41
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Yanî ew ji navê Receb bûye?
 
Meaning it comes from the name Receb?

42
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Receb bûye. Receb bixwe ji Çomazin e.
 
It was Receb. Receb himself is from Çomazin.

43
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Û qeçkên Receb çar in. Yek jê re digotin Hem. Yek jî Nas.
Yek jî Henan. Yek jî His. Evana qeçkên Raca ne.
 
And Receb has four sons. One was called Hem. And one Nas.
And one Henan. And one His. These are the sons of Raca.

44
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Û Raca bixwe, hat çû ji Çomazin. Raca bixwe ji Çomazin
derket.
 
And Raca himself came and went from Çomazin. Raca himself
left from Çomazin.

45
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Û hat çû li hafiya Rûtê, kaniya Rûtê rûnişt.
 
And he came and settled by the edge of Rûtê, the Rûtê
spring.

46
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Ji wir jî hat, dibêjin yek ji mezinên me, dibêjin hat çû li
gundê Raca rûnişt, hafiya Raca û li ser kaniya Raca bixwe.
 
From there he also came, one of our elders says, he came and
settled in the village of Raca, the edge of Raca, right on
the Raca spring itself.

47
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Û çar lawê wî Raca hene, wek ku min te re gotî, nava çar
lawên wî, His û Henan û Hem û yek jî Nas.
 
And Raca had four sons, as I told you, among his four sons,
His and Henan and Hem and also one Nas.

48
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Ev li kû rûniştin? Evna di gundan de ne. Hemî di gundan da
ne, bes qeçkên xwe hene, qeçkê qeçkan hene, li vê derê.
 
Where did they settle? They are in the villages. They are
all in the villages, but they have their children, their
children's children, here.

49
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Em bixwe ji Hemê ne.
 
We ourselves are from Hemê.

50
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Malbat tenê ev in? Giştî yek in, wek ku me di gundê din de
dîtin malbat gişt yek in.
 
Are these the only families? Are they all one, just as we
saw in the other village, where the families are all one.

51
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Bes du mal di nav me de li vir de ji derveyî gund hatine.
 
Only two families among us here came from outside the
village.

52
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Hinek dibêjinê Şera, yek jî mala Bekirê Reşo ji Gurda hatine
vir derê. Evna ne ji Raca ne.
 
Some are called Şera, and also the Bekirê Reşo family came
here from Gurda. These are not from Raca.

53
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Bes mezinên wan heft, deh... em dibînin mirî hene.
 
But their elders, seven, ten... we see they have deceased
here.

54
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Ê naha hejmara gund, çiqas mal e?
 
And now what is the population of the village, how many
houses?

55
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Gund teqrîben pêncî - şêst mal e.
 
The village is approximately fifty to sixty houses.

56
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Û Êlî Caro?
 
And Êlî Caro?

57
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Êlî Caro jî weha jî şêst - heftê mal heye, çil mal e...
 
Êlî Caro also has about sixty to seventy houses, forty
houses...

58
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Yanî gund sed û bîst, sed û deh... sed û bîst, yan nagihîje
sed û sî malî.
 
So the village is a hundred and twenty, a hundred and ten...
a hundred and twenty, or it doesn't reach a hundred and
thirty houses.

59
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Em gişk bi hev re, şahiya be, li miriya be, em gişk bi hev
re ne.
 
We are all together, whether in joy, or for the deceased, we
are all together.

60
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Komîn wek ku Mustefa got komîna me yek e, gundê me yek e, em
gişk li ba hev in.
 
The commune, as Mustafa said, our commune is one, our
village is one, we are all with each other.

61
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Erê, gişk yek in, em ba hev in.
 
Yes, all are one, we are with each other.

62
00:05:46,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Mala we ava be. Em ê naha derbasî nav herdu gundan bibin.
Spas ji we re.
 
Bless your homes. We will now pass through both villages.
Thank you.

63
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Gundê Êlî Caro û Raca girêdayî navçeya Mabeta ne, nêzî
pazdeh kîlometreyî li rojavayê navçeyê dikevin.
 
The villages of Êlî Caro and Raca are connected to the
Mabeta district, situated about fifteen kilometers west of
the district.

64
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Gundê Êlî Caro û gundê Raca bûne yek gund. Û malên wan
gihîştine hevdu.
 
The village of Êlî Caro and the village of Raca have become
one village. And their houses have reached each other.

65
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Goristan, dibistan û komîna wan yek e. Gundê Êlî Caro û Raca
li ser çiyayekî bilind hatine avakirin.
 
Their cemetery, school, and commune are one. The villages of
Êlî Caro and Raca have been built on a high mountain.

66
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Û di nava herêmeke çiyayî de ne. Ev çiya bi darên zeytûnan
xemilandî ne.
 
And they are located in a mountainous region. These
mountains are adorned with olive trees.

67
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Her wek tê gotin, ku di demên borî de hemî daristanên merxê
bûn, û ta naha hinek daristan li derdora gund hene û hawire
derên wişînkatiyê xemilî ne.
 
As it is said, in the past they were all pine forests, and
even now there are some forests around the village, and
their surroundings are adorned with greenery.

68
00:06:51,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Navê gundê Êlî Caro ji navê kesekî bi navê 'Elî Jaro'
hatiye, ji Eliyê Jaro teter bû, û wî çar kur hebûn: Hec
Birîm, Os, Ehmed, û Şêx.
 
The name of the village of Êlî Caro comes from a person
named 'Elî Jaro'; Elî Jaro was a courier, and he had four
sons: Hec Birîm, Os, Ehmed, and Şêx.

69
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Bi vî awayî ev gund mezin dibe. Gundê Êlî Caro ji 60 xanî
pêk tê, û nêzî 500 kes lê dijîn.
 
In this way, this village grew. The village of Êlî Caro
consists of 60 houses, and nearly 500 people live there.

70
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Navê gundê Raca ji kesekî bi navê Raca Çomazin hatiye.
 
The name of the village of Raca comes from a person named
Raca Çomazin.

71
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Ku ev kes di demên zêrîn ên gund de tê nas kirin an ku kesê
yekemîn li gund nîştecîh bûye.
 
This person is recognized in the golden times of the
village, or as the first person to settle in the village.

72
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Tê gotin ku sê kurên Raca hebûn. Yek jê bi navê Raca li vira
ma.
 
It is said that Raca had three sons. One of them named Raca
stayed here.

73
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Yê din jî çû li gundê Sewliyê li navçeya Efrînê nîştecî bû.
 
Another one went and settled in the village of Sewliyê in
the Afrin district.

74
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Yê sêyemîn bi navê Hemê Raca li devereke nêzî Raca nîştecîh
bûye. Û nav lê bûye gundê Raca.
 
The third one named Hemê Raca settled in a place near Raca.
And it was named the village of Raca.

75
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Sê malbatên bingehîn di gundê Raca de hene. Osê, Hemê Raca,
û malbata Wahîd.
 
There are three main families in the village of Raca. Osê,
Hemê Raca, and the Wahîd family.

76
00:07:55,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Ango bi giştî dora 90 xanî, û nêzî 1300 kes li her du gundan
dijîn. Û her du gund mîna gundekî ne.
 
Meaning altogether there are around 90 houses, and nearly
1300 people living in both villages. And both villages are
like one village.

77
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, di gundê Êlî Caro de jî em derbas cem
mixtar bûn, cem Apê Remzî.
 
Yes, dear viewers, in the village of Êlî Caro we passed by
the headman, Uncle Remzî.

78
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Naha em ê bi hev re Apê Remzî jî nas bikin. Apê Remzî
leşkeriya Fransa kiriye. Merheba Apê Remzî.
 
Now we will get to know Uncle Remzî together. Uncle Remzî
served in the French military. Hello, Uncle Remzî.

79
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Ehlan wa sehlan.
 
Welcome.

80
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Apê Remzî, emrê te çiqas e, sal e?
 
Uncle Remzî, how old are you, in years?

81
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Welle nizanim. Ev dewrê şer, ev wêladî min, ez nizanim
tiştekî min tûne.
 
I swear I don't know. During the era of war, this birth of
mine, I don't know, I have nothing.

82
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Dema ku tu bûyî leşker, te eskeriya Ferensa kir, tê bîra te?
Te di kîjan salê de kir?
 
When you became a soldier, you did the French military
service, do you remember? In which year did you do it?

83
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Erê, dema emrê me bû hevdeh hejdeh bîst bûn... hewqasî,
dewletê Tirkiyê rabûyî mat e.
 
Yes, when our age was seventeen, eighteen, twenty... around
that much, the Turkish state had risen and caused a
stalemate.

84
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Em bûne eskerê Fransa, û min çar salan ji eskeriya Fransa re
kir.
 
We became soldiers for France, and I did military service
for France for four years.

85
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Te li ku derê kir, te li kîjan alî da bû, yanî di nav de
nêzîkî kû derê bû?
 
Where did you do it, on which side were you, meaning inside
near where was it?

86
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Li wê derê... li Efrînê, li Ezazê, heta bi Çobanbegê, heta
bi Cerablusê... Min wê derê, mintaqeyan eskerî kir.
 
Over there... in Afrin, in Azaz, all the way to Çobanbey,
all the way to Jarablus... I served in the military there,
in the regions.

87
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Yanî tê bîra te, tu di kîjan wextî de bû, kîjan salê da bû?
 
Meaning, do you remember, what time it was, what year it was
in?

88
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Eeee... De ya rabê kî dibêje, çixwe salan dipirsin, ji esasê
we dipirse, êdî her kesek diçe kîfa xwe.
 
Uhhhh... So by God whoever says it, they just ask the years,
he asks about your origins, now everyone goes on their own
way.

89
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Te çar salan eskerî kir?
 
You served in the military for four years?

90
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Çar salan min ji Fransa re eskerî kir.
 
I did military service for France for four years.

91
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Ê hevalên te yê wê demê kî bûn, ji gundê we kes hebû, ji wê
herêmê heye?
 
And who were your friends of that time, was there anyone
from your village, is there anyone from that region?

92
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Ji gundê me, welle di herêma me de tune ne.
 
From our village, I swear there's no one in our region.

93
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Ji kû derê hebûn?
 
Where were they from?

94
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Ji mintaqê hebûn... ji mintaqa Bilbilê hebûn.
 
There were some from the region... there were some from the
Bilbil region.

95
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Wê demê yanî wek ku te got xeyrî te kesek ji aliyê Fransa re
eskerî nekir?
 
At that time, so as you said, apart from you no one did
military service for France?

96
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Ji topraxa min xeyrî min, kesî ji Ferensa re eskerî nekir.
 
From my land apart from me, no one did military service for
France.

97
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Ê tu di wê demê da, leşkerîya te xweş bû...
 
And you at that time, was your military service pleasant...

98
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Dema ku Kurdî min pirsbûn, te digot ew ê kirin, Fransa
kirin?
 
When I asked about the Kurds, you were saying they did it,
France did it?

99
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Ê Kurmanc di dest de hebûn, pirr bûn.
 
Yes, there were Kurmanjs in their hands, they were many.

100
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Ê Kurmanc, demek eskaderonekî wer ra digotin eskaderon Kurd
lêcê...
 
The Kurmanjs, I mean, there was an esquadron they called
Escadron Kurde Léger...

101
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Nav lê nan, wextê ku herbê Çolaq ra kirin, Fransa herbê
Çolaq ra kirin...
 
They named it that, when they fought the war against Çolaq,
France fought the war against Çolaq...

102
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Çolaq neşkandin, nekuştin. Çolaq kuştin...
 
They couldn't defeat Çolaq, they didn't kill him. Çolaq
killed...

103
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Rabûn, kirin eskaderon Kurd lêcê lêxa. Sey ke.
 
They got up, and made the Escadron Kurde Léger hit. Look.

104
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Yanî, Kurmanc li mêra dixin, heta bi Fransa, bi ewa kirin.
 
I mean, Kurmanjs fight like men, even the French, they did
it with them.

105
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Yanî negotin Çolaq Kurmanc kuştin, gotin eskaderon Kurd lêcê
lêxa.
 
I mean, they didn't say Çolaq killed the Kurmanjs, they said
the Escadron Kurde Léger hit.

106
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Yanî çi maneyê didê ev?
 
So what does that mean?

107
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Yanî manesiya xwe, Kurmanc li mêra dixin.
 
It means, Kurmanjs fight like men.

108
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Kurmanc mêrxas in, di şecaetê de.
 
Kurmanjs are brave, they are courageous.

109
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Ev mistaşarê Fransa ev laqab da ewa, da Kurmanca.
 
This French advisor gave them that title, to the Kurmanjs.

110
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Ê dema ev şer çêbû, tu ji Çolaq tê bîra te?
 
And when this war happened, do you remember Çolaq?

111
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Ne tê bîra min, bes wextê şuxlê digotin mezinên me waha.
 
No, I don't remember, but when they talked about the events,
our elders (told us) this.

112
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Wextê ku Çolaq herbê bike, hat ji milê çepê ra derbaz bû.
Demek ji milê çepê yê Çolaq derbaz bû.
 
When Çolaq came to fight, he came and passed from the left
side. It means he passed from the left side of Çolaq.

113
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Ê çû Çolaq ê mir. Topraqê Çeqel a mir. Li wê derê kuştin.
 
Çolaq went and died. He died on the land of Çeqel. They
killed him there.

114
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:50,000
De wê demê da Çolaq bi Miheddînê Îbşoşê bû, de wê demê ev ne
li hember Fransa şer kirin?
 
So at that time Çolaq was with Miheddînê Îbşoşê, at that
time didn't they fight against France?

115
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Na, na, na, Miheddînê Îbşoşê berî wê. Berî wê. Berî Çolaq a.
Miheddînê Îbşoşê.
 
No, no, no, Miheddînê Îbşoşê was before that. Before that.
Before Çolaq. Miheddînê Îbşoşê.

116
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Ê ewî jî li hember Fransa şer kir?
 
He also fought against France?

117
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Ewî j'kir.
 
He did too.

118
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Yanî ê destpêkê şer li hember Fransa kirî, Miheddînê Îbşoşê
bû?
 
So the first one to fight against France was Miheddînê
Îbşoşê?

119
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Ê, paşê Çolaq kir. Çolaq, demek de ewe da, digerî, digerî
Qemraşê da, digerî ew da... kir.
 
Yes, then Çolaq did. Çolaq, I mean in that area, touring,
touring in Qemraşê, touring there... he did.

120
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Ê piştî wê tu bûyî eskerê Fransa?
 
And after that, you became a French soldier?

121
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Piştî wê em bûn eskerê Fransa.
 
After that, we became French soldiers.

122
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Demek hevdû birakî wî bû, birakî Çolaq bû, ew di nav kuştin.
Paşê ew kuştin, paşê Çolaq kuştin.
 
It means he was his brother, he was Çolaq's brother, they
killed him in it. Then they killed him, then they killed
Çolaq.

123
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Demê da askeriya xwa pirr bûn?
 
During your military service, were there many of you?

124
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Demek wê çaxê askerî Kurmanc tayîn kiribûn ji qereqolê hatin
li Çolaq xistin. Ji paş ra hatin.
 
It means at that time they had appointed Kurmanj soldiers,
they came from the outpost and hit Çolaq. They came from
behind.

125
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Yanî wê demê da ji qereqola hatin...
 
I mean, at that time they came from the outpost...

126
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Ji qereqola hatin.
 
They came from the outpost.

127
00:12:54,000 --> 00:13:07,000
Demek wê çaxê Fransa, askerê xwe, eskaderonek wê... yanî
eskaderon wê çaxê... sed esker...
 
It means at that time France, its soldiers, an esquadron of
it... I mean an esquadron at that time... a hundred
soldiers...

128
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Wê çaxê ji paş ra hatin li Çolaq xistin.
 
At that time they came from behind and hit Çolaq.

129
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Ji Încîrlê da hilkişîn, hatin Çolaq kuştin. Ji wê...
duduyan... ji paş ra hatin li Çolaq xistin, Çolaq kuştin.
 
They went up from İncirli, they came and killed Çolaq. In
that... the second... they came from behind and hit Çolaq,
they killed Çolaq.

130
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Çi tê bîra te, hîna ew demê da, wê demê da çi salî bûyî?
 
What do you remember, still from that time, what age were
you at that time?

131
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Demek wê çaxê hîna em yanî ameyî di di deh sal, di yanzdeh,
di donzdeh, di sêzdeh sal, panzdeh sal wê çaxê, ew wext tê
bîra min.
 
It means at that time we were still... I mean around ten
years old, eleven, twelve, thirteen years, fifteen years at
that time, I remember that time.

132
00:13:49,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Û wê demê te got ez çûme Cerablusê ji wê demê da... we şer
li hember kesî kir? Te şer nebû qet?
 
And at that time you said I went to Jarablus at that time...
did you fight against anyone? Did you never fight?

133
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Na, me şer nekir. Bûn di mexferek, tayîn dikirin tu keve
herî mesela Çoban Beg, tayîn ke carek herî Cerablusê, ji
Fransa weha tayîn ji Fransa de diçêbûn.
 
No, we didn't fight. We were at an outpost, they would
appoint you to go to, for example, Çobanbey, appoint you
once to go to Jarablus, from France like this, appointments
were made by France.

134
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Fransa demek dirêj li vir ma? Tê bîra te dema ji vir
derketî, çûyî?
 
Did France stay here for a long time? Do you remember when
they left here, when you went?

135
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Wextê ji vir derketî... wextê j'vir derketî... hefta sal
bim, demek li Cerablusê bûm.
 
When they left here... when they left here... I must have
been seventy, I mean I was in Jarablus.

136
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Dema Fransa ji vir çû, tu j'Cerablusê vegeriya hatî vir?
 
When France left here, you returned from Jarablus to come
here?

137
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
E...
 
Yes...

138
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Dema Fransa j'vir çû, di çil û şeşan da vegerî, çû?
 
When France left here, in forty-six they returned, they
left?

139
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Kurmancan ew nekir. Qena Ereb a kirin.
 
The Kurmanjs didn't do it. But the Arabs did.

140
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Kurda li hember Fransa kirin?
 
The Kurds did it against France?

141
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Nê, Kurda kirin.
 
No, the Kurds did it.

142
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Kî bû ew demê da?
 
Who was it at that time?

143
00:14:54,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Demek wê çaxê Raşîd Îbo hebû, Miheddînê Îbşoşê, paşê Çolaq
hat... pê ra hatin Kurmanc. Demek Miheddînê Îbşoşê, berî
Çolaq e. Na berî, berî ye.
 
It means at that time there was Raşîd Îbo, Miheddînê Îbşoşê,
then Çolaq came... Kurmanjs came with them. It means
Miheddînê Îbşoşê is before Çolaq. No, he is before, before.

144
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Ew eskerê wextê Fransa kirine... di çiyayê Kurmênc da... tu
navê wana nas dikî, kî bûn ew?
 
Those soldiers during the French time... in Kurd Mountain...
do you know their names, who were they?

145
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Kî? Na ew mirin e. Hinek ji Şiyê hebûn, ji Bilbilê hebûn.
 
Who? No, they died. There were some from Şiyê, there were
some from Bilbilê.

146
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Ji Qitmê hebûn. Ekseriyet ji Qitmê û ji Qurtqulaqê Mezin...
Ekseriyet ji Qurtqulaqê Mezin û Qitmê bûn.
 
There were some from Qitmê. Mostly from Qitmê and Big
Qurtqulaq... Mostly they were from Big Qurtqulaq and Qitmê.

147
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Ehmed Şêxo bû ji Qitmê?
 
Was Ehmed Şêxo from Qitmê?

148
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Ehmed Şêxo ji Qurtqulaqê Mezin, ew Ehmed Şêxo bû, Birok
hebû, Bedrî... Birok jî hebû.
 
Ehmed Şêxo was from Big Qurtqulaq, that was Ehmed Şêxo,
there was Birok, Bedrî... there was also Birok.

149
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Ê piştî Fransa te çawa bûyî mixtar?
 
So after France, how did you become a mukhtar?

150
00:15:55,000 --> 00:16:04,000
Ji roja Hafiz Esed girtiye dest ez mixtar im.
 
From the day Hafez al-Assad took power, I have been a
mukhtar.

151
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Yanî çil û pênc sal e?
 
So it's forty-five years?

152
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Çil û pênc sal e.
 
It's forty-five years.

153
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Te mixtarê şeş gunda yî?
 
You are the mukhtar of six villages?

154
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:29,000
Erê... Alî Caro yek, Me'serkê didu, Birka sê, Raco çar,
Mist'eşûra pênc. Hemî şeş gund in wa, û Çomazna.
 
Yes... Ali Jaro is one, Me'serkê is two, Birka is three,
Raco is four, Mist'eşûra is five. They are all six villages,
and Çomazna.

155
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Te mixtarê şeş gunda yî?
 
You are the mukhtar of six villages?

156
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

157
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Û heta niha tu mixtar î?
 
And you are still the mukhtar until now?

158
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

159
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Serkeftin ji te ra.
 
Success to you.

160
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Ê mixtar, dema tu bûyî mixtar heta niha navên gundên me ji
hatin guhertin? Yanî dema dewleta Sûriyê ji gundên nav...?
 
Well mukhtar, when you became a mukhtar until now, have the
names of our villages also been changed? I mean, during the
time of the Syrian state, did they change the village
names...?

161
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Sûriyê ji guhertin. Yanî gundên wa mesela Alî Caro. Alî Caro
asas e. Esasê gund e.
 
Syria also changed them. I mean their villages for example,
Ali Jaro. Ali Jaro is the original. The original of the
village.

162
00:16:51,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Tirkî lê danîbûn... ew Tirkî. Mesela gundek hene, Me'serkê,
Me'sere lê kirin, 'k' rakirin.
 
They had put Turkish on it... that's Turkish. For example,
there's a village, Me'serkê, they named it Me'sere, they
removed the 'k'.

163
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Ê navên gundên me heme çar caran hatine guhertin. Destpêkê
Kurmancî bû, piştî wê Roman hat, Aramiya danîsa nav
guhertin, Tirk hat dîsa guhertin, Sûriyê hat dîsa guhertin.
 
The names of our villages have been changed four times in
total. First it was Kurmanji, after that the Romans came, in
Aramaic they changed the names again, the Turks came and
changed them again, Syria came and changed them again.

164
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Bes gund wek berê mane. Wek nav wek berê mane.
 
But the villages have remained as before. As names, they
have remained as before.

165
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
Wek berê mane.
 
They remained as before.

166
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Yanî her demî hinek hatin navê gundên me guhertin.
 
I mean, in every era, some people came and changed the names
of our villages.

167
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

168
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Ê mala te ava bî. Spas ji te ra.
 
May your home prosper. Thank you.

169
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Ehlen û sehlen, mît selam, ser çava.
 
Welcome, a hundred greetings, upon my eyes.

170
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Ser çava.
 
Upon my eyes.

171
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Her du gundên hev a têkilî û peywendiyên baştane.
 
The two villages have a good relationship and connection.

172
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Di aheng, şahî û xemgîniyan da bi hevdu re alîkar in û destê
xwe didin hevdu.
 
In harmony, joy, and sorrow, they help each other and lend
each other a hand.

173
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Xelkên her du gundan da bara xwe bi çandiniyê dikin.
 
The people of both villages mostly make their living from
agriculture.

174
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Mîna hemû gundên navçeyê, darên zeytûnê berhemên sereke ne.
 
Like all the villages in the sub-district, olive trees are
the main product.

175
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Li gel zeytûnan, darên fêkî jî têne çandin.
 
Along with olives, fruit trees are also planted.

176
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Mamosta, merhaba, çawa yî?
 
Teacher, hello, how are you?

177
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Merhaba. Silav. Ser serê min, ser çavê min.
 
Hello. Greetings. Upon my head, upon my eyes.

178
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Spasdar im. Em destpêkê te nas bikin.
 
Thank you. Let's get to know you first.

179
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Ethem... ji Alî Caro.
 
Ethem... from Ali Jaro.

180
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Spasdar im ji te re, ser çavên min.
 
Thank you, upon my eyes.

181
00:18:53,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Niha, ev gelî bi vê bîrê tê naskirin, wekî te behs kir. Ev
bîra, çend gund li ser av dibirin? Çend gund av ji vê bîrê
dibirin yanî?
 
Now, this valley is known by this well, as you mentioned.
This well, how many villages took water from it? I mean, how
many villages got water from this well?

182
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Vê bîrê, bîra heft gundan bû berê. Heft gundan dihatin av
dibirin. Me'serkê, Birka, Çomaznê, Raco, Mist'eşûra... hinek
xasman ji derdorê dihatin av ji vê bîrê dibirin.
 
This well, it was the well of seven villages before. Seven
villages used to come and take water. Me'serkê, Birka,
Çomaznê, Raco, Mist'eşûra... some specific ones from the
surroundings would come and take water from this well.

183
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:31,000
Av berê tune bû. Bes niha li gundan giyan bîr çêbûn. Herkes
bi ava xwe derbas dibe. Ev bîr jî wisa mehcur mane wek vî
halî.
 
There was no water before. But now, wells have been built in
all the villages. Everyone gets by with their own water.
This well has also remained abandoned like this in this
condition.

184
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Me ha îsal jî wisa da... yek komînek ava kir, wekî yek komîn
me hazir kir...
 
This year too, we did this... we established a commune, like
a commune we prepared it...

185
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Yanî wek komîn...
 
I mean, like a commune...

186
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:47,000
E komîn, me çêkir... komîna gund me, ev kir, me çêkir, me
hazir kir.
 
Yes a commune, we formed it... our village commune, did
this, we built it, we prepared it.

187
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Ev gundên ku te behsa wê kir, niha Mist'eşûra li ku derê
dikeve? Ev gundan, ji ber ku dema em derbasî gundê we bûn,
Mist'eşûra ji vir nedihat dîtin.
 
These villages you mentioned, where is Mist'eşûra located
now? These villages, because when we entered your village,
Mist'eşûra wasn't visible from here.

188
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,000
Mist'eşûra hew ji vir nêzîk e. Di gelî ra nêzîk e, dihatin
ji vira, bi dewar dihatin av dibirin.
 
Mist'eşûra, it is close to here. It's close through the
valley, they used to come from here, they came with animals
taking water.

189
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Û ev gelî jî hemî bi vê bîrê tên naskirin?
 
And is this whole valley also known by this well?

190
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Ev bîr a kî ya ve ne? Navê bîrê çi ye?
 
They are all known by this well, the Well's Valley.

191
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Ev bîr a kî ya ve ne? Navê bîrê çi ye?
 
Whose well is this? What is the well's name?

192
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Bîra Kevê ye, nexêr bîr a Omer e. Bîra Romaniyan, em rêt xwe
pir dirêj e.
 
It is the Kevê well, no, Omer's well. The Roman well, its
life is very long.

193
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Kes nizanî çi wexta ye.
 
No one knows what time it is from.

194
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Bes roman. Berî Selahedîn e. Selahedîn hezar sê sed sal e,
vê bîrê û vê darê çinarê ev e hezar sê sed sal teqrîben
heye. Yanî.
 
Just Roman. Before Saladin. Saladin is 1300 years old, this
well and this sycamore tree are approximately 1300 years
old. I mean.

195
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Ev cihê Kurda ye piştî wî ye?
 
Is this a place of Kurds after him?

196
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Ev cihê Kurda ye tabiî.
 
This is a place of Kurds, of course.

197
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Berê roman jî kurd bûn, duyê roman hîn jî kurd in.
 
In the past Romans were also Kurds, during Roman times they
were still Kurds.

198
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Belê belê.
 
Yes, yes.

199
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Na te behsa darê kir, ev dar a çi dar e? Çinar e?
 
Now you talked about the tree, what kind of tree is it?
Sycamore?

200
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Çinar e, ha.
 
Yes, a sycamore.

201
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Te got emrê wê çiqas e?
 
You said how old it is?

202
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Hezar sê sed sal e.
 
1300 years old.

203
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Çi kesî dîrokî nivîsandina wê kesî yanî kesî jê mişext
kiriye?
 
Did anyone write about its history, meaning, has anyone
recorded it?

204
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Na, na.
 
No, no.

205
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Bi devkî hatiye gotin?
 
Has it been passed down orally?

206
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
A bi gotina, bi gotin hatiye gotin.
 
Yes, through spoken word. It has been passed down orally.

207
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Ev dar a jî, çiqas bilindbûna wê heye?
 
And this tree, how tall is it?

208
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:55,000
Qalindiya wê? Bilindbûna wê teqrîben pêncî metir bilindbûn
zêdetir heye. Bes milet hat qut kirin. Ejng qut kirin, da
qut kirin.
 
Its thickness? Its height is approximately 50 meters, maybe
more. But people came and cut it. They cut off branches,
they cut the wood.

209
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Dar pir mezin bû.
 
The tree was very big.

210
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Dar pir mezin bû. Di vê berê jî golik diçû kokê darê ra...
 
The tree was very big. In the past a calf would go into the
root of the tree...

211
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Na hezar ta mînim holê darê de belê, yanî halî hîn vekiriye.
 
Now a thousand can stay in the hollow space of the tree,
yes, I mean it's still open.

212
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Vekiriye.
 
It's open.

213
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Vekiriye.
 
It's open.

214
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Na ev kela ku dar e çi ye, ev mehser e?
 
Now, this stone structure where the tree is, what is it, a
mill?

215
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Ev hava meqbes e, zeytûn çêdikirin berê. Paşê jî girtin û
ne, û ev a tînim avê...
 
This is a press, they used to process olives here in the
past. Then they closed it and no, and I bring this to the
water...

216
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Mehser e yanî.
 
It's a mill, then.

217
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,000
Mehser e.
 
It is a mill.

218
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Mamoste de hem te got, başqa bîr a vî hene? Tine ne?
 
Teacher, you also said, are there other wells like this? Are
there not?

219
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Tine ne, na.
 
There aren't any, no.

220
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Ev tenê, av jî tê de heye?
 
Just this one, does it also have water?

221
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Tê de jî av. Hîn ku ava xwe koşk nabe.
 
It also has water. Its water never dries up.

222
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Û biharê ava ti diçêle de, ta biharî meha şeşan.
 
And in the spring the water falls, until the spring of the
sixth month.

223
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Meha pêncan, meha şeşan dimîne hişk dibe.
 
The fifth month, the sixth month it stays and then dries.

224
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Ne hişk nabe, ava kaniyê qut dibe. Derdikeve yanî.
 
No, it doesn't dry up, the spring water stops. It stops
flowing, I mean.

225
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Ev ava baranê ye yanî? Ne keve bîrê ra?
 
So this is rainwater? Doesn't it fall into the well?

226
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Na ava baranê nakevê.
 
No, rainwater doesn't enter it.

227
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Av a jêr çate. E çay e.
 
It's underground water. It's a spring.

228
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,000
E mala te ava be. Spas ji te ra.
 
May your home prosper. Thank you.

229
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Mala te jî ava, ser serî min û ser çavê min, hatina we pir
biha ye ji me ra. Spas...
 
May yours prosper too, you're very welcome here, your visit
is very precious to us. Thanks...

230
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,000
Saeta te xweş.
 
May you be well.

231
00:21:55,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Saeta te jî xweş, ehlen wa sehlen, ser serî min...
 
May you be well too, welcome, you are very welcome...

232
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Li biniya gundê Alî rojava bîrekê ... ava heyî, bi navê Bîra
Alîceran tê nas kirin.
 
Below the village of Ali to the west of a well... containing
water, it is known as the Alicer Well.

233
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:15,000
Xelkê herêm gundan av jê dibirin, û pezên xwe jî av didan.
 
People from the regional villages used to take water from
it, and also watered their sheep.

234
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:20,000
Û ta niha, di hemû demsalan de ava xwe dimîne.
 
And even now, it retains its water in all seasons.

235
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Û biharê de, dibe cihê geşt û seyranê.
 
And in the spring, it becomes a place for outings and
picnics.

236
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:39,000
Apê Xelîl merheba êvar baş.
 
Uncle Xelil, hello, good evening.

237
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:44,000
Ya helî, ya helî, merheba, mala we ava, ronî, ahlen wa
sehlen.
 
Oh welcome, welcome, hello, may your home prosper, light,
welcome.

238
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Sax bî. Apê Xelîl, em dibînin em her gundekî em digerin
tiştekî wan yê balkêş, çi hebe, kesekî necar be, yanî çi kar
li gundî de hebe em çêdikin.
 
Stay healthy. Uncle Xelil, we see that in every village we
visit, if there is something interesting, whatever it is, a
carpenter, I mean whatever work there is in the village we
cover it.

239
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:55,000
Em derbasî gundê we li Alcaran bûn, me behsa te kirin.
 
We passed by your village in Alcaran, and they told us about
you.

240
00:22:55,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Ser serê min û ser çavê min re, hatine we ser serê min û ser
çavê min re.
 
You are very welcome here, your arrival is an honor to me.

241
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Sax bî. Gotin tu necar î, me got em derbasî ba te bibin.
 
Stay healthy. They said you're a carpenter, we said let's
visit you.

242
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Belê. Mî selame ... ahlen wa sehlen. Bi xêr hatin.
 
Yes. Greetings... welcome. Welcome.

243
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Sax bî. Apê Xelîl ka ji berê de tu çi çêdikî û nuka wa tu çi
çêdikî ji berê da?
 
Stay healthy. Uncle Xelil, tell us what you made in the past
and what you make now compared to the past?

244
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:20,000
Ji berê da, hesîncaran çêdikim, ez kêra çêdikim, ez bî
cerceran çêdikim, ji berê da, yanî min çêdikirin, da te
zanî? Erê wey.
 
From the past, I make blacksmithing tools, I make knives, I
make threshing sleds, from the past, I mean I used to make
them, you know? Yes.

245
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Ê tu ji kê elimî, tu ji kê fêr bû?
 
And who did you learn from, who taught you?

246
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:29,000
Ez ji kesî fêr nebûm, ji kesî ne elimîm, e me bi nerînê ye,
min bi nerînê na haliyan axaçi binirim pê xudî yekî wekî wî
çêkim.
 
I didn't learn from anyone, I wasn't taught by anyone, it
was through watching, through watching I can now just see
something and make one like it myself.

247
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Ebeden. Ez ji kesî ne elimîme, e gî bi çavê xwe me elimiye.
 
Not at all. I didn't learn from anyone, I learned all of
this with my own eyes.

248
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Yanî di gund da ji malbata te da kes necar tenabû?
 
I mean in the village, in your family no one was a
carpenter?

249
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:45,000
Na, di aîla me de kes jî necar tenabû, bes em bi nerînê, ya
piyê xwe tu çi dixwaze, tu çi dixwaze binihêrî bave avê e ev
şixulê min a.
 
No, in our family no one was a carpenter, but just by
watching, you see whatever you want, you watch what you
want, father, that is my work.

250
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,000
Te bi xwe, pîşeya xwe jî girt.
 
You yourself adopted your own craft.

251
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Pîşeya xwe jî girt.
 
I adopted my own craft.

252
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:49,000
Her bijî eştere.
 
Long live the master.

253
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Sax bî, seta te xweş be.
 
Stay healthy, may you be well.

254
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Sax bî, te got te cercer çêdikrin?
 
Stay healthy, you said you made threshing sleds?

255
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

256
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Naha dibêjin cercer pirraniya wan jî nemane?
 
Now they say the majority of threshing sleds are no longer
here?

257
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,000
Na. Tine ne. Kêm in.
 
No. They don't exist. They are rare.

258
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:02,000
Ê cercer çend sal berê yanî ta bihê vî ko derê cercer bûn?
 
So threshing sleds, how many years ago were they around...
where were threshing sleds?

259
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:14,000
Belkî 40 sal pêş, 40 sal heye, 35, 40 heye, nemane. Vana
dirase derketin, deh de derketin. Hawa dewiya cercera dar a
mir.
 
Maybe 40 years ago, it's been 40 years, 35, 40, they are
gone. These combine harvesters appeared, ten appeared. And
so the wood of the threshing sleds died.

260
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Şixulê berê, me dawêr bar dikirin, me qantir dikirin di avê
da diçûn av dikişandin şixulê bar dikirin.
 
The old work, we used to load cattle, we used mules, they
went in the water and drew water, they loaded the old work.

261
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:27,000
E xweşbûna gundê berê çiqas xweş bû, ew mal ser hev dera
bûn, bi hev ra gundî bi xwe bi hev ra dibûn alîkar.
 
And how nice the village charm was in the past, those houses
were close together, the villagers themselves helped each
other.

262
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Bi hev ra kar dikirin, bi hev ra misade dikirin, cercer ...
 
They worked together, they assisted each other, threshing
sleds...

263
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Karê yekî xelas bûya, mesele li bêdera xwe xelas bûya, ê
cîranî te, yê meriyê te çunî te man, nedihişt tu xwe bîrê
xwe bikare.
 
When one person's work was finished, for example, he
finished his threshing floor, your neighbor, your relative
stayed with you, he wouldn't let you work on your well by
yourself.

264
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Na te keviyê re, har gêr dikira, û yê gundî jî ava dikira,
yanî hawa jî, jêra bi xwe re ra dikira.
 
He wouldn't leave you alone, he would start threshing, and
the villager would process it too, meaning, he would raise
it up for himself with him.

265
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Yanî bi rastî, cercer dê tê bîra min jî wez biçûk bûm. Ji
gund riş debû, yanî me dît çewa cercer wî wextê xelkê demê
derbas dikirin. Hema sitran jî digotin. Jîran bi hev re
dibûn alîkar.
 
I mean honestly, the threshing sled also comes to my mind
when I was young. It was prevalent in the village, I mean we
saw how people spent their time with the threshing sled back
then. They even sang songs. Neighbors helped each other.

266
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

267
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:59,000
Yanî xweşbûnek pir xweş bû, ev rojên wisa pir xweş bûn.
 
I mean it was a very beautiful charm, those days were so
beautiful.

268
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,000
E te başqa çi çêdikir?
 
And what else did you make?

269
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:10,000
Me çi çêdikir başqe? Wek necarîya me tê da heştî, heşt tişta
çêdikir, der çêdikir, wekî çi çêdikim.
 
What else did we make? Like our carpentry, we made eighty,
eight things, doors, whatever I can make.

270
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:15,000
Apê Xelîl demê tu çêdikî te dîsa tenê li vî cî da çêdikir,
te li gund çêdikir? Tu li kûderê çêdikir?
 
Uncle Xelil, when you were making them, did you only make
them here in this place, did you make them in the village?
Where did you make them?

271
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:26,000
Me li gund çêdikir, di mal da min çêdikir. Ez biçûma cût,
ez, ez cût haterm... sê çara hecî hewşê na. Da tu zanî.
Behsa tenê bû.
 
We made them in the village, I made them at home. When I
went to plow, I, I would drive the plow... you'd see three
or four things in the yard. You know? They weren't
discussed.

272
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:27,000
Te cût dikir?
 
Did you plow?

273
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Lê, me cût dikir, ez cût dihatim, hefter car, sê çara tişkî
di dîn li hewşê min çêkirine av a ne. Xudanê xwe da hatin
pereyê xwe didan, dibirin.
 
Yes, we plowed, I returned from plowing, seven times, three
or four crazy things in my yard I made these. Their owners
came, paid their money, and took them away.

274
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:43,000
Apê Xelîl naha te da te behsa cût kir, cawan gelek cawan e,
ew, ew çi zehmetî da hebû?
 
Uncle Xelil, now you talked about plowing, youths, there are
many youths, what difficulty was there in it?

275
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Ew zehmet ... Xa wê zehmet wê çaxê zehmet pir bû, yanî
radbûn pir bû, ne wekî nuha ko. Niha alet bi derketin, ha
derketin nabe te rehet bî, te rehet nabe.
 
That difficulty... The difficulty of that time was very
hard, I mean, waking up was a lot, not like now. Now
machines have appeared, things have appeared, you can't be
comfortable, you can't be comfortable.

276
00:25:55,000 --> 00:26:02,000
Yanî çiqas zehmet bi vî cewana... çawa bavê me û kalsêrê
kezinî, rîspiyên me ev ciwanane girtin weke dan û kirin darê
zeytûnê?
 
I mean how hard it was for these youths... how did our
fathers and elders, our wise ones, take these youths in hand
and plant olive trees?

277
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:11,000
Ew kupçiya va kir... Kupçî hatin, zemanekî kupçî hatin, bi
pîçokê kolan û gişk derfet kirin gişk ava kirin, av kirin.
 
The excavators opened them... Excavators came, there was a
time excavators came, they dug with a scoop and opened up
everything, built everything, watered it.

278
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:13,000
E wê demê de gişk zeytûn çandin.
 
And at that time they planted olives everywhere.

279
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:17,000
Lê, paşê zeytûn çandin, dar çandin, av kirin.
 
Yes, later they planted olives, planted trees, watered them.

280
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:19,000
E çiqas zehmetî bû ye?
 
And how difficult was it?

281
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:28,000
E zehmet bû. Ew çaxê traktor tunebûn, cût bû, cûtê dewêr
bûn, pir erê pir radibûn, pir bûn. Ne wekî nuka...
 
It was difficult. At that time there were no tractors, there
were plows, cattle plows, it took a lot of effort, they woke
up a lot, there were many. Not like now...

282
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Bes xweşbûna wê demê da wisa... wekî hûn wekî xwe em wisa
dibînin xweş bûn e. Ê ev cêrîtiyê, ev hûtên kevir ev cûtên
dehl evan ev derxistin holê ma, tiştekî gelek zehmet e wê
demê da we çêkiriyê, di nifşê din yê nûha nifşê nûha na kes
nabe...
 
But the charm of that time, like... as you yourself, as we
see it, it was nice. This bravery, those stone plows, those
field plows, they brought these out, it is a very difficult
thing you did at that time, in another generation, the
current generation, no one can...

283
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Wella we deme xweş bûn, nê?
 
Well, that time was nice, no?

284
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,000
E şîrîn bûn rehet bûn.
 
They were sweet, they were comfortable.

285
00:26:51,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Şîrîn bûn, rehet bûn. Bi hevra mistade dikirin.. evê dawêr,
serekê cûtî dawêr... naha nûka, hiliyan emrê min heftê sal
e. Sibê heta êvarî evê ez çêdikim, heta êvarê wekî ez nuka
ez jê aciz nabe...
 
They were sweet, they were comfortable. They helped each
other.. these cattle, the head of the cattle plow... now
currently, I'm 70 years old. From morning to evening I make
this, until the evening like now I don't get tired of it...

286
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Xêr e, xwaş e. Dawar ku di pêşiya te, te cût dikir tu
keyfxweşiyê pê ra dibînî, of dibînî tolazkî difetile
sekiniye sersêşki dibe.. da tu zanî, ê nuka kil patoze are,
av dikin dar û ber.
 
It is good, it is nice. When the cattle was in front of you,
you plowed and found joy with it, oh you see a young lad
spinning, standing up, head spinning.. so you know, and now
it's fallen to the thresher and such, they process wood and
stones.

287
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Gî xera kirin da tu zanî. Herin jor û jor da du bil kin axên
xwarin av dikin ... axê jî da xistin binê û kevir bûn jor.
Yanî ne wekî vî çaxê cûtî dawêr e ew ...
 
They ruined everything, so you know. They go up and up, push
twice, process the food soils... they also put the soil down
and the stones came up. I mean not like this time of cattle
plowing and that...

288
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,000
Em vegerin ser karê te.
 
Let's return to your work.

289
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:20,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

290
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:24,000
Naha tu pêşiya me pir tişt hene, tu dikarî tu bi xwe behsa
ser karê xwe dên kî?
 
Now you have many things in front of us, can you yourself
talk about your work?

291
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:35,000
A. Hawa tomax e, me'nê zeytûna, me'nê pîrê ku... pîrek me ji
bo zeytûna bişkîne, ji bo zeytûna ye.
 
Yes. This is a mallet, meaning for olives, meaning an old
woman who... our old woman to break olives, it is for
olives.

292
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Û ev ha jî çirk e ye. Ev a, zemanê berê mehnî kumirkî ya evê
avê, wekî vî ha holkê ye me te zanî? ev ha darî ye.
 
And this is a churn stick. This, in the old times, meant a
coal... this water, like this bucket here, do you know? This
is its wood.

293
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Hawa xwedî kirin, di şit da tu da şixuliya ba ... yanî çiqas
xwar ba hinek ew dê ev dara ra dikir ... ev da wê bî.
 
They raised it like this, if you had worked on it... I mean
no matter how crooked it was, someone would have
straightened this wood... it gave it.

294
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:59,000
Û ev ha kefçî ne... me'nî şîv bûn. Ev ha jî mehnî dew bû. Ev
di wê demê da hemî kefçî ê dar bûn.
 
And these are spoons... meant for soup. And this meant for
yogurt drink. During that time, all spoons were made of
wood.

295
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Ê dar bûn, çêdikirin...
 
They were made of wood, they made them...

296
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,000
Ev kîjan dar û tişt ...
 
These which wood and things...

297
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,000
Tabîyet kîjan dar e?
 
What wood is it characterized by?

298
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:10,000
Hawa darê qetlebî ye. Ev a kefçî mehnî şîv av e me çêdikirin
jinê bi şîv tavdidan, av dikirin.
 
This is arbutus wood. This spoon is meant for soup, we made
them, women stirred soup with it, processed it.

299
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:11,000
Hey naha bi kar tînin?
 
Are they still using it now?

300
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Erê hey, na wey, hey na bi kar tînin, yanî ê xwe di şixul ê
de tehmel bi ka, a bi xêr, tu ji hez diki avkî, te kefçî di
dar dî şîvê xwe tav da, ji pakiya xwe e we vaye nuka ketiye
aliminyon ev in ...
 
Yes they do, no wow, yes they use them now, I mean if you
work with it carefully, bless you, if you like to use water,
if you stir your soup with a wooden spoon, it is for its
purity, now they pour aluminum on these...

301
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:33,000
Tame tiştê nîne bîni tiştê nîne.
 
It has no taste of anything, no smell of anything.

302
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:37,000
E ew tişt di karê min, te çi tişt bi destê xwe çêkiriye?
 
And that thing in my work, what have you made with your
hands?

303
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:38,000
Van min bi destê xwe çêkirin.
 
I made these with my hands.

304
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:40,000
Erê van me dît te bi destê xwe çêkiriye?
 
Yes, we saw you made these with your hands?

305
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:45,000
Belê belê... Û ev ha jî kefçî ... darê qetlebî ne... Me'nî
dew av... ev ê biçûktir e ev ji mazin e...
 
Yes, yes... And these are also spoons... of arbutus wood...
Meaning for yogurt drink, water... this is smaller, this is
bigger...

306
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,000
O mezin jî hene.
 
Oh, there are also big ones.

307
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:48,000
O mezin jî hene.
 
Oh, there are also big ones.

308
00:28:48,000 --> 00:29:02,000
Û ev ha me'nê, min çêkiriye ev ha ... ferûc e. Ne te zani,
ferûc hinek di nav ser tiştê caw, ta cê kî da pîçeka goşt
lêxe, av bike, seke çawa bi tiştê dike, tiştekî ...
 
And this means, I made this... it's a mallet. So you know, a
mallet, someone puts it on top of the fabric, you made it so
she hits a little piece of meat, process it, watch how she
hits the thing with it, something...

309
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:03,000
Yanî ji bo goşt e.
 
So it's for meat.

310
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:05,000
Ji bo goşt e ha.
 
For meat, yes.

311
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:14,000
Û van, kêr e, min çêkir, me'nî malê, koşkê me xwaş e jî kir
em ehtiyacî tişta der nebin. Seke çi qas tûj e.
 
And these, knives, I made them, meaning for home, our corner
is nice, so we don't need things from outside. Look how
sharp it is.

312
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Pir tûj e.
 
It's very sharp.

313
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Ha wisa ne, ev jî me çêkirin.
 
That's how it is, we made these too.

314
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Ev ha jî te çêkiriye. Ev a?
 
You also made this. This one?

315
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Ev ha kurik e, ev ha îşta kêra pê çêdikirin e esna pê dikin
îra.. sor dikin.. esn te sor nekir çê nabe.. westa me pênca
di cih nebin.. te sor kir asen te sor nekir ... maşe bi kar
tanî te bînî cî alî dikane... min sor dikir.
 
This is a mallet, this is for making knives they use it..
they heat it.. if you don't heat the iron it won't work.. if
we don't have pliers in place.. you heat it, if you don't
heat the iron... you use a tong to bring it from the shop's
side... I used to heat it.

316
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,000
Hawa jî ors e. Ne te zani?
 
This is an anvil. So you know?

317
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:36,000
Dest xweş keremê te bî...
 
Good job, bless you...

318
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Hawa ors e. Ev ha çakûç e. Madi da ne ser mi min pê
çêdikira.
 
This is an anvil. This is a hammer. They put it on my
shoulder and I worked with it.

319
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Ev a huceta te ye bî...
 
This was your tool...

320
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:58,000
Ee min pê çêdikir vana. Ev ha matqeb e. Vana, rîşe ha ne,
bolad e di hava ne. Te zani? Ti kefçîyekî wê meqî e tişta ha
vana bal e haw ... bes tu pê xurt dikî ve dikî ew a min pê
çê dikirin, ev dikirin ...
 
Yeah I worked with these. This is a drill. These, here's a
drill bit, there is a blade inside it. You know? If you
wanted a spoon of this... these things have a blade
inside... enough, you push with it and open it, these I
worked with, did these...

321
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Na Apê Xelîl...
 
Now Uncle Xelil...

322
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:03,000
Gelo di hemî deran de qet we tiştek wilo nedît? Min delîbek
dît.
 
Did you ever see something like this anywhere else? I saw a
"delîb".

323
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,000
Ev delîba we çêkiriye we bi xwe çêkiriye, yan kesî din
çêkiriye?
 
This "delîb" you built, did you make it yourselves, or did
someone else?

324
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:10,000
Welleh delîb ketiye reşê. Berê çêdikirin.
 
Well, the "delîb" has fallen into disuse. They used to make
it.

325
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Xelkê kevir hebin. Ê kavirên reş çêdikirin avadikirin.
 
People used stones. They used to build it with black stones.

326
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:17,000
Qicikêd malê, xilfê me hebûn li kûran, wan çêdikir.
 
The children of the house, we had servants at the deep
places, they used to build it.

327
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:20,000
Da ku di nav de tiştan veşêrin û çêbikin. Nizanî?
 
So that they can hide and make things inside it. You know?

328
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:23,000
Ew kaviran çêdikirin û weha ... çêdikirin.
 
They made those stones and like this... they made them.

329
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Kevirên binî, vêra dibêjin "sinî", ha ew siniya binî ye.
 
The bottom stones, they call them "sini" (tray), that is the
bottom tray.

330
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:27,000
Yanî ne te çêkiriye?
 
So you didn't make it?

331
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Na, min çênekiriye. Naxêr, kevir hebûn wan çêdikirin.
 
No, I didn't make it. No, there were stones, they used to
make them.

332
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:33,000
Qicikên malê, xilfên... Ebdiyê malê, xilfên wî, wan çêdikir.
 
The children of the house, the servants... the Abdi of the
house, his servants, they used to make it.

333
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,000
Belê ... wilo ye.
 
Yes... that's how it is.

334
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:37,000
Berê we çû gundekî, hûn gundê Qurnê bûn, rast e?
 
Before you went to a village, you were in the village of
Qurnê, right?

335
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Yekî ji min ra got ku li gundê we yekî delîba çêkiriye,
yanî.
 
Someone told me that in your village someone made a "delîb".

336
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Erê... Paşê em ketinê me ax dikişand. Ax, darên ku em
dikişandin...
 
Yes... Then we started, we were dragging dirt. Dirt, the
wood we were dragging...

337
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Darên merxê em dikişandin, me ew dikişand... Me çêdikir.
 
We were dragging pine wood, we dragged it... We made it.

338
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:53,000
Yanî me sîware çêdikirin, bi dewar... Dewarê gundan, bi
dewar bûn.
 
I mean we made walls, with animals... Village animals, it
was with animals.

339
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Hîn jî li gundan hene?
 
Are there still any in the villages?

340
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:56,000
Hene lê... Tev hene.
 
There are, but... There are many.

341
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:57,000
Belê... hene.
 
Yes... they exist.

342
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Ma tu bi xwe çêkiriye?
 
Did you make it yourself?

343
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Na, me tu tişt çênekiriye.
 
No, we didn't make anything.

344
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,000
Spas ji we re, saeta we xweş.
 
Thank you, have a good time.

345
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Saeta te jî xweş be, Xwedê ji te razî be ya reb.
 
Have a good time too, may God bless you, oh Lord.

346
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Bi silametî bin.
 
Stay safe.

347
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:11,000
Spas.
 
Thanks.

348
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Li başûrê herdu gundan, gundê Mistka Şûra û Çiyayê Eloyê
Omê.
 
In the south of the two villages, the village of Mistka Şûra
and Çiyayê Eloyê Omê.

349
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:23,000
Yekûyek bi dar û berên merxê, rengê kesk di hemû demsalan de
li xwe dike, dixemile.
 
It is entirely adorned with pine trees and wood, wearing the
color green in all seasons, decorated.

350
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:25,000
Û li bakurê gund, Birc Qaşan e.
 
And in the north of the village is Birc Qaşan.

351
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:29,000
Li rohilatê gund, Çomêzina ye, ew jî nêzîktirîn gund e.
 
In the east of the village is Çomêzina, which is also the
closest village.

352
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:49,000
Û li rojavayê gundê Şiketa ye.
 
And in the west is the village of Şiketa.

353
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Belê temaşevanên Hêja. Di gundê Raco de, em rastî malekê
hatin, ew jî êzingan hûr dikin.
 
Yes, dear viewers. In the village of Raco, we came across a
family who are chopping wood.

354
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Naha zivistan e, amadekariya xwe ji sobê re dikin. Naha em ê
bi hev ra nas bikin, merheba apê min.
 
Now it's winter, they are preparing for the stove. Now we
will get to know them together, hello uncle.

355
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:27,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

356
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:28,000
Em dikarin hev nas bikin?
 
Can we get to know you?

357
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Bi Remzî navê min...
 
My name is Remzi...

358
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:31,000
Ser çavan apê min.
 
Nice to meet you, uncle.

359
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Navê min Henan e.
 
My name is Henan.

360
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Ser çavê min.
 
Nice to meet you.

361
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Hûn ji kû derê ne? Ji Raco ne?
 
Where are you from? From Raco?

362
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:36,000
Belê em ji Raco ne.
 
Yes, we are from Raco.

363
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Îro em di nav gundê we û gundê Hecara de digerin. Em rastî
we hatin, we jî êzing hûr dikirin.
 
Today we are walking around your village and the village of
Hecara. We ran into you, and you were chopping wood.

364
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:45,000
Kesê ku hûr dike, em ê wî jî nas bikin.
 
The person chopping, we will get to know him too.

365
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Heysem.
 
Heysem.

366
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:50,000
Navê te Heysem e? Kurê Remzî ye. Ser çavê min.
 
Your name is Heysem? He is Remzi's son. Nice to meet you.

367
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:52,000
Destê we sax bin, spasdar im.
 
Bless your hands, thank you.

368
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:56,000
Naha dema êzinga ye. Zivistan e.
 
Now is the time for firewood. It is winter.

369
00:32:56,000 --> 00:33:02,000
Di destpêka zivistanê de sermayek çêbû... Amadekariya xwe
dikin ku têxin sopeyê da...
 
At the beginning of winter it got cold... They are preparing
to put it in the stove...

370
00:33:02,000 --> 00:33:08,000
Berê... berê da, dema we êzing tanîn, berî sobe hebûn, we
çawa dikir?
 
Before... in the past, when you brought firewood, before
there were stoves, what did you do?

371
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:13,000
Berê da tenê kalkê me êzing tanîn. Dema qorê kelan... me
êzing tanîn.
 
In the past, only our grandfather brought firewood. When it
was time for boiling... we brought firewood.

372
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Lê berê sobê tune bûn. Çal hebûn, di nav çalan de wan agir
dadikirin.
 
But before there were no stoves. There were pits, they lit a
fire in the pits.

373
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:22,000
Dirûvê qelê bû di bedena wan de. Kûnik kûnik xwîn
derdiketin... xelkê bi kincên xwe ve diçûn ser poxarê,
bitirsa tu poşmaman nebe.
 
It was like a fry in their body. Blood was coming out in
drops... People would go over the smokehouse with their
clothes on, afraid of getting sick.

374
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Ew ji bo poxarê bû. Bê guman!
 
That was for the smokehouse. Of course!

375
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:30,000
Diket nava poxarê û li wir dima. Dûyê reş radibû ... Bi ber
poxarê ve dibû mîna rûyê min reş diçû dihat ... Ew wisa bû.
Belê!
 
They went into the smokehouse and stayed there. Black smoke
rose... by the smokehouse their faces would get black like
mine going back and forth... That's how it was. Yes!

376
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:31,000
Ma gelo xelk tev de wisa bûn?
 
Were all the people like that?

377
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,000
Belê, xelk giş wisa bûn!
 
Yes, all people were like that!

378
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Ma ji ber sermayê we ev yek dikir?
 
Did you do this because of the cold?

379
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:47,000
Belê me germ dikir. Berê wek niha germ nedibû, ew a niha ku
em germ dibin ... diçûn li devê kûran rûdiniştin germ dibûn,
diçûn germ dibûn ...
 
Yes, we warmed up. It wasn't warm like it is now, the warmth
we get now... they went and sat at the edge of the kilns and
warmed up, they went to warm up...

380
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:50,000
Berê we digot odeyêd berê tijî ferş bûn.
 
In the past you used to say the old rooms were full of rugs.

381
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:55,000
Erê ferş bûn. Berê, nola niha, nola wê çaxê, ew ferş bûn, ew
tenê hebûn.
 
Yes, they were rugs. Before, unlike now, like that time,
they were rugs, that's all there was.

382
00:33:55,000 --> 00:34:05,000
Xaniyên dîrokî bûn. Tîran ew xaniyên axê girtin. Pêşî, ez
herim, em li axê bûn...
 
They were historic houses. Beams held up those mud houses.
First, let me tell you, we were on dirt...

383
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:09,000
Erdê di hundir de di bin xestî de dema baran dihat hundir
germ dibû.
 
The ground inside, under the felt, when it rained, it got
warm inside.

384
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:15,000
Û paşê ... Bi dora xwe de dihatin rûniştin. Me ji ber ku bi
xirecira rûniştinê...
 
And then... they would sit around it. Because we were
bustling with sitting...

385
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Em bi cih cuda bûn û dihatin rûniştin, bi wê cîhê xwe ...
 
We separated our places and sat down, in that place of
ours...

386
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:24,000
Derbas dikirin, piştî derbasbûnê de çûn, bîna ecêb bûn,
mazot hat ...
 
They spent time, after the time spent they went, strange
things happened, diesel came...

387
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Me dest bi anîna mazotê kir... tiştên zêde bûn.
 
We started bringing diesel... more things happened.

388
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Lê sobeyên êzingan hîn jî mane yan na?
 
But do the wood stoves still exist or not?

389
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Belê mane! Paşê derbas bûn, ... fakihet (fêkî) zivistanî mûz
dîtin, mûz ...
 
Yes they do! Then they passed... they saw winter fruits like
bananas, bananas...

390
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Hêjîr nedîtin ... hêjîr dîtin, mişmiş dixwarin ...
 
They didn't see figs... they saw figs, they ate apricots...

391
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:49,000
Hêjîr dixwarin, mişmiş dixwarin, kuncî bi rûn lêdidan û
dixwarin... Fakiheta zivistanî ev bû.
 
They ate figs, they ate apricots, they poured oil on sesame
seeds and ate them... These were winter fruits.

392
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Kehrebê berî çend salan gihîşt gund?
 
How many years ago did electricity arrive in the village?

393
00:34:52,000 --> 00:35:00,000
Kehrebe teqriben, ez bibêm, berî bîst yan pênc û bîst salan
li gundên me heye.
 
Electricity roughly, I'd say, arrived twenty or twenty-five
years ago in our villages.

394
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:01,000
Ne zêde ye.
 
Not that long ago.

395
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Na ne zêde ye.
 
No, not that long.

396
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:07,000
Berê we çawa dikir? We êvaran çawa bi ser dikir? Bi çirayê?
 
What did you do before? How did you spend your evenings?
With lanterns?

397
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:19,000
Bi çirayên xazê ... berî fanos hebûn. Hîn di wê demê de em
fanos bi gazên xwe ve digirt û diçûn, me ew li aleman didît.
Me destê xwe wisa dikir, destê me reş dibû. Em li dîwarî
dixist, me qaziq lêdixist.
 
With kerosene lanterns... before there were lamps. Even at
that time we took lamps with our own gas and went out, we
saw it everywhere. We did this with our hands, our hands got
black. We hit it against the wall, we hit it with a stake.

398
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Dûre ... me çêdikirin... ew cî bi kehrebe bûn yanî ...
 
Then... we used to make it... those places had electricity I
mean...

399
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:29,000
Bi wê çirayan em derbas dikirin. Û di hundir de jî ronî bû,
hundir mazî bû, me nedîtibû ...
 
We spent time with those lanterns. And inside it was also
bright, the inside was oak, we hadn't seen...

400
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:35,000
Me ji mezinên xwe bihîst... digotin kilfet giş nav hev da
bûn, wek noka tek-tek tune bû yanî ...
 
We heard from our elders... they said women/children were
all together, not scattered one by one like now...

401
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:45,000
Giş di nava hundir de rûdiniştin. Çira bûn û dûv re kehrebe
hat. Em giş fêrî bûn.
 
They all sat inside. They were lanterns and then electricity
came. We all got used to it.

402
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:47,000
We luks jî bikar dianî?
 
Did you use Lux lamps as well?

403
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:55,000
Diçûn, berî fanosan çira bûn, diçûn ser agir ... îskender,
îskenderûnê ...
 
They went, before lamps there were lanterns, they went to
the fire... Iskender, to Iskenderun...

404
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Gelek dûr e.
 
It's very far.

405
00:35:56,000 --> 00:36:04,000
Diçûn, wan çirayên gazê ... bişev çûna Iskenderûnê. Kesek
diçû ... dema peyda dibû... bi peyatî diçûn... heta sala...
70, sala 70yan.
 
They went, those gas lanterns... traveling to Iskenderun at
night. Someone would go... when it was available... they
went on foot... until the year... '70, year 1970.

406
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:13,000
Paşê fîşke hat. Ew fîşke jî wan dixistin kuncê poxarê de, du
fîşke dixistin hev du da, pê fîşke dikirin ku em pê ra ronî
dibin...
 
Then the matchstick came. They would put those matchsticks
in the corner of the smokehouse, they'd put two matchsticks
together, striking them so we could light up with them...

407
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Ev tişt tê bîra we?
 
Do you remember these things?

408
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:19,000
Na tê bîra me. Lê em negihaştin wê demanê, em gihan
demanê...
 
No we remember. But we didn't reach those times, we reached
the time of...

409
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:21,000
Hûn gihiştibûn dema luks û wan tiştan.
 
You reached the time of Lux lamps and those things.

410
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:21,000
Paşê we luks anîn.
 
Yes yes, we reached that time.

411
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:22,000
Paşê we luks anîn.
 
Then you brought Lux lamps.

412
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Erê paşê çira bûn.
 
Yes then there were lanterns.

413
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:27,000
Naha, piranî li gundê we sobeyên êzingan e an sobeyên mazotê
ne?
 
Now, is it mostly wood stoves or diesel stoves in your
village?

414
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:28,000
Na mazot nîne, giş êzing e!
 
No there's no diesel, it's all wood!

415
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:33,000
Hemiya dar li ba wan hene?
 
Does everyone have wood with them?

416
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:34,000
Hene!
 
Yes!

417
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:36,000
Naha, ji berê da, sobeyên êzingan, li ba we hene.
 
Now, since a long time, you have had wood stoves with you.

418
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:41,000
Berî poxar bû, ji poxarê da, naha sobeyên êzingan bûn...
 
Before it was a smokehouse, since the smokehouse, now there
are wood stoves...

419
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Gelo tu bi taybetî kîjan daran hildibijêrî da ku têxî
hundir, zeytûnê...
 
I wonder if you specifically pick out certain woods to put
inside, like olive...

420
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:53,000
Zeytûn zû vêdikeve. Darê sîngan e... darê mişmiş e, behîv e,
hejîr nîn e!
 
Olive burns quickly. Peg wood... it's apricot wood, almond,
not fig!

421
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Ew nakeve de.
 
That doesn't go in.

422
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Ew nabin êzing.
 
That doesn't become firewood.

423
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Ka ev darên çi ne?
 
So what kind of wood is this?

424
00:36:56,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Ev ê zeytûnê ne. Zeytûn û gûzan e ...
 
This is olive wood. It's olive and walnut...

425
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:02,000
Ev dar e.
 
This is wood.

426
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:03,000
Erê!
 
Yes!

427
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:05,000
Û di her malekî de sobeyên êzingan heye?
 
And there is a wood stove in every house?

428
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Di her malê de sobeya êzingan heye.
 
There is a wood stove in every house.

429
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:13,000
Te dît, di destpêkê de sobeyên êzingan dihatin çêkirin, ji
Efrînê û her weha ji bajarê Tirmişoyê dihate, ew pir nêzîk
bûn...
 
You saw, in the beginning wood stoves were made, it came
from Afrin and also from the city of Tirmişo, they were very
close...

430
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Erê wan çêdikirin. Ev sobeyên êzingan... wan çêdikir.
 
Yes they used to make them. These wood stoves... they used
to make them.

431
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:19,000
Piştî wê de... bajêr dihat çêkirin... Her kesekê sobeyek
çêdikir, ev sobeyên ...
 
After that... the city made them... everyone made a stove,
these stoves...

432
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:22,000
Niha pircureyan çêdikin, cûrbecûr çêdikin. Pircure çêdikin
...
 
Now they make a lot of types, they make various types. They
make a lot of types...

433
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:24,000
Em silavên xwe didin Heysem jî.
 
We give our greetings to Heysem as well.

434
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:24,000
Ebbûre, Heysem...
 
Talk!

435
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:28,000
Ebbûre, Heysem...
 
Ebbure, Heysem...

436
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:30,000
Merheba şirê min.
 
Hello my boy.

437
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:32,000
Ehlen û sehlen. Te bixêr hatî.
 
Welcome. Welcome to you.

438
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Sax be. Welleh kurê min te zahmetî dikişîne... sermaye ye.
 
Stay well. By God, my son, you are working hard... it is
cold.

439
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Em tiştok nakin, ewan nekin em ê ji sermê ra bimirin.
 
We don't do much, if we don't do those we will die from the
cold.

440
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Lê, baş e... te çend rojan van êzingan hûr kirî?
 
But, alright... for how many days did you chop this
firewood?

441
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Welleh teqrîben bû 3-4 roj in, ez ê wan bixistima hundir,
min evana xelas kir û ew man.
 
By God, it was roughly 3-4 days, I was going to put them
inside, I finished these and those remained.

442
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Me wan ji bo zivistanê amade dikin.
 
We prepare them for winter.

443
